{"body":{"branch_id":"B1","constraint_refs":[{"id":"record:sha256:5cd8e98fce09ce65555018c1603e0ca13338f827ae649e45d99fbf4c1f0a664e","kind":"constraint","required":true,"schema_version":"eidomancer.record.schema.v0.2"},{"id":"record:sha256:f86741b38d0e7389442cfe21a02e550c47cf13d6a2de30641f91c47ee3522e29","kind":"constraint","required":true,"schema_version":"eidomancer.record.schema.v0.2"},{"id":"record:sha256:c86e7aa7975793289b0e8307b22a48856332fad7a8b8aa7e8d4190dfa120d612","kind":"constraint","required":true,"schema_version":"eidomancer.record.schema.v0.2"}],"creator_operation_ref":{"id":"record:sha256:e457e692ae7daf1cfde604bc7a686a58b8bed4a87810db2afb7c1d57a54a0b04","kind":"operation","required":true,"schema_version":"eidomancer.record.schema.v0.2"},"description":"With the shutter still open, one amber crawler crosses from the amber chamber into the blue chamber while one blue crawler crosses in the opposite permitted direction, from blue into amber. The remaining amber crawler stays in the amber chamber, and the remaining blue crawler stays in the blue chamber. This produces a balanced exchange: each chamber now contains one amber crawler and one blue crawler. Once both crossings are complete, the shutter is closed permanently. The timing makes the mixed distribution deliberate rather than accidental: closure occurs only after the two directional transfers have finished, so neither crawler is caught needing a prohibited return crossing. After closure, the chambers become permanently isolated with respect to passage travel. Each side therefore retains representatives of both kinds, but the original same-kind pairings are split across the irreversible barrier. Any later activity must proceed within the chamber where each crawler was located at closure, making the coordinated exchange a lasting structural feature of the burrow.","facts":{"amber_in_amber":1,"amber_in_blue":1,"blue_in_amber":1,"blue_in_blue":1,"shutter_closed":true},"intelligence_response_ref":{"id":"r